Interval Regular expression 
these expression tell us about the number of occurences of a character in a string 

expression        description
{n}             matches the preceding character appearing 'n' times exactly 
{n,m} minimum , max occurances 


{m,}
minimum  m ocurences and max no limit 


Usecase: 
name should contain min of 2 character 
name should contain only alphabets 

[a-zA-Z]{2,}

[0-9]{10} =>any 10 digit number 
[6-9][0-9]{9} ==> mobile number should start with 6 to 9 

egrep [6-9][0-9]{0} sample.txt 
egrep "[0-9]{10}" sample.txt 

